# Keep secrets and local state out of the Docker build context.
#
# The Dockerfile copies backend/ wholesale, so without this file a local
# `docker build` bakes backend/.env -- the database URL, JWT secret and every API
# key -- into the image. Render builds from the git checkout, where .env does not
# exist, so this matters most on a developer's machine, which is exactly where
# an image is most likely to be pushed somewhere it should not be.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local databases and their backups.
**/*.db
**/*.db.bak*
**/*.sqlite*

# Nothing the API image uses.
.git
**/__pycache__
**/node_modules
mobile/
marketing/
